<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Italian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was the unified Italian state proclaimed in 1861 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, lasting until the republic was established in 1946. It built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> through colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. The name Italian is also used across the site for Italy, its peoples and its earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/city-state">city-states</a>, which appear in many other empire profiles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Italy" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Italian Empire emerged from the ambitions of the <b>Kingdom of Italy</b>, newly unified in the Risorgimento and proclaimed in 1861 and completed with the capture of Rome in 1870.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The new state lasted until Garibaldi's Expedition of the Thousand in 1860 and its annexation to the <b>Kingdom of Italy</b> in 1861.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The new state kept the Sardinian constitution, army, administration and dynasty, and even its regnal numbering, and historians usually treat the <b>Kingdom of Italy</b> as the Kingdom of Sardinia renamed and enlarged.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>At the encounter of Teano Garibaldi met King Victor Emmanuel and handed him the conquered kingdom; the people voted in a plebiscite to join the Kingdom of Sardinia, and the annexation completed the first phase of Italian unification, the <b>Kingdom of Italy</b> being proclaimed in 1861.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1859–1860 the Romagna rebelled, the papal army was defeated at Castelfidardo, and the Marche and Umbria voted to join the new <b>Kingdom of Italy</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>After further changes of ruler under Napoleon and Austria, Venice joined the <b>Kingdom of Italy</b> in 1866.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
